\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{3y}{4}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =-\\frac{3y}{4} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${x}^{2}=-3y.$" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292941 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292942 13194139534520 true] [17592186292941 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534520 true] [17592186292941 1041 "field-1" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292941 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292942 13194139534520 true] [17592186292941 1110 #uuid "e99c9df6-f2cc-5ed9-a171-8462a5376590" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292942 1034 "-3y" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292942 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292942 1111 #uuid "1f803e75-9b26-5e64-a1d6-7b797e1d6f4b" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292943 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292944 13194139534520 true] [17592186292943 1089 "q-84713" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292943 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534520 true] [17592186292943 1100 "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=8x?$" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292943 1113 #uuid "a9145c40-11b6-5c53-84a9-a35178e11e5a" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292943 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =8x \\\\ 4p & =8 \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(2){t}^{2},\\,y=2(2)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{2},\\,y=4t.\n$$" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292945 13194139534520 true] [17592186292944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292946 13194139534520 true] [17592186292944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292947 13194139534520 true] [17592186292944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292948 13194139534520 true] [17592186292944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292949 13194139534520 true] [17592186292944 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534520 true] [17592186292944 1041 "selection" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292944 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292946 13194139534520 true] [17592186292944 1110 #uuid "6c7489d0-5022-5856-a7a9-edd1a1b530fc" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292945 1034 "x=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=t" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292945 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292945 1111 #uuid "117bc97b-159e-5f39-ae0b-5622a3e8cdd5" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292946 1034 "x=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292946 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292946 1111 #uuid "9c782378-7a17-5bfd-8b36-6ecb1e1ae9f0" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292947 1034 "x=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=2t" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292947 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292947 1111 #uuid "7f2d9e68-a412-52df-bab4-bbe886a1f0f4" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292948 1034 "x=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292948 1111 #uuid "fd7cd036-f557-5ad8-80f5-2d359137642c" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292949 1034 "x=4{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292949 1111 #uuid "25faf918-8669-5623-96c0-13e9863656c2" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292950 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292951 13194139534520 true] [17592186292950 1089 "q-84716" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292950 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534520 true] [17592186292950 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030835/assets/85894c676349da1794c2b4e3ab3add867fbe9e91037bee060e3592039c3850cf.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292950 1113 #uuid "bce7fc99-bd19-5e4a-b792-a3131930ed98" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292950 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(-4,4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-4,4),$ we can substitute $x=-4$ and $y=4$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 4=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ 2 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -4 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(-1){t}^{2},\\,y=2(-1)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-{t}^{2},\\,y=-2t.\n$$" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292952 13194139534520 true] [17592186292951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292953 13194139534520 true] [17592186292951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292954 13194139534520 true] [17592186292951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292955 13194139534520 true] [17592186292951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292956 13194139534520 true] [17592186292951 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534520 true] [17592186292951 1041 "selection" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292951 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292956 13194139534520 true] [17592186292951 1110 #uuid "3211c247-545e-56e6-8770-74f762989612" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292952 1034 "x=-2t,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292952 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292952 1111 #uuid "abf67c92-8439-5da3-ad32-3da71bae0baa" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292953 1034 "x=-{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-t" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292953 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292953 1111 #uuid "ae81af5a-897c-57ba-8234-a67aeaa3bd01" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292954 1034 "x=-2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-t" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292954 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292954 1111 #uuid "c9f03f2d-b0f2-5cc9-8aef-0a322494a651" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292955 1034 "x=2t,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292955 1111 #uuid "89da28e5-b2d4-5d5d-a1af-c408847123e4" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292956 1034 "x=-{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=-2t" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292956 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292956 1111 #uuid "e40f87dc-ceb0-574a-a0b2-21274b385970" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292957 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292958 13194139534520 true] [17592186292957 1089 "q-84732" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292957 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534520 true] [17592186292957 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3{t}^{2},\\,y=6t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292957 1113 #uuid "ed5bc52d-bb18-523c-9f90-f507332dc970" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292957 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{x}{3},\\,t=\\frac{y}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{x}{3}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =\\frac{x}{3} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =12x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${y}^{2}=12x.$" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292959 13194139534520 true] [17592186292958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292960 13194139534520 true] [17592186292958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292961 13194139534520 true] [17592186292958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292962 13194139534520 true] [17592186292958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292963 13194139534520 true] [17592186292958 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534520 true] [17592186292958 1041 "selection" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292958 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292963 13194139534520 true] [17592186292958 1110 #uuid "804885a6-7eac-53cc-82bc-50894af38ab2" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292959 1034 "{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}x" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292959 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292959 1111 #uuid "b45ce23d-deea-5ff7-96e3-9653a68a49c3" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292960 1034 "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}x" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292960 1111 #uuid "32678392-1bba-5f12-8f68-7faff3019212" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292961 1034 "{y}^{2}=x" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292961 1111 #uuid "1f86edc9-61b4-536a-9240-09ba49787893" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292962 1034 "{y}^{2}=6x" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292962 1111 #uuid "244f01a1-6ea3-5947-b99b-1fba8ffc55a9" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292963 1034 "{y}^{2}=12x" 13194139534520 true] [17592186292963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534520 true] [17592186292963 1111 #uuid "6ff5b688-26ff-5bb0-b5dc-41961fc7548b" 13194139534520 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-106421" 17592186292933 "q-106421/selection" 1